        <h2>What does a psychiatric provider do?</h2>
        <p>People sometimes know they want "a psychiatrist" but aren't sure what type of care they actually need.</p>
        <p>Psychiatric care can include evaluation, diagnosis, medication management, treatment planning, and ongoing follow-up. Some people seek care for the first time, while others already have a diagnosis and are looking for continued medication management.</p>
        <p>Whether medication is appropriate is something you can discuss with your provider. Treatment is individualized rather than one-size-fits-all.</p>
