        <h2>Do I need a psychiatrist, therapist, or psychiatric provider?</h2>
        <p>These roles can overlap, but they are not identical.</p>
        <p>A therapist or counselor may be a good fit if you are primarily looking for psychotherapy and support with emotional, behavioral, or relationship concerns.</p>
        <p>A psychiatric provider may be appropriate when you are looking for psychiatric evaluation, medication management, or ongoing medical management of a mental-health condition.</p>
        <p>You can also work with both. Many patients see a therapist for ongoing psychotherapy while working with a psychiatric provider for medication management.</p>
        <p>If you already have a therapist, you do not necessarily have to start over. With your permission, your providers can coordinate care when appropriate.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pill"><i class="fa-solid fa-users" aria-hidden="true"></i><div><h3>Not sure what's right for you?</h3><p>We're happy to help you explore your options.</p></div></div>
